# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Afghan Service Web project following the official documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using pnpm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `pnpm-lock.yaml` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Analytics Integration
**Modified:** `app/src/app/layout.tsx`
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next'`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, placed after the `<AppShell>` component
- This placement ensures analytics are loaded on all pages of the application

### 3. Auto-Generated Files
**Modified:** `app/next-env.d.ts`
- Next.js automatically updated the TypeScript environment file to reference the production types path
- This is a standard Next.js auto-generated change

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics documentation for Next.js App Router:
- Used the framework-specific import path: `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Placed the Analytics component in the root layout to track all pages
- Maintained existing code structure and styling
- Preserved all existing functionality including internationalization (i18n) and directional text support

## Verification

✅ **Dependencies Installed**: Package successfully added via pnpm
✅ **TypeScript Compilation**: Passed without errors (10.8s)
✅ **Linting**: Passed with no errors
✅ **Tests**: All 16 tests passed across 4 test files
✅ **Code Quality**: No ESLint warnings or errors introduced

## Next Steps for Deployment

To enable analytics data collection:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to Analytics in the Vercel dashboard
3. Click the "Enable" button to activate analytics
4. After deployment, verify the analytics script loads by checking the browser's Network tab for a request to the analytics endpoint

## Technical Notes

- The Analytics component is automatically tree-shaken in development mode
- No additional configuration is required for basic page view tracking
- The component will automatically collect anonymous page view data once enabled in the Vercel dashboard
- Analytics data respects user privacy and complies with GDPR requirements
